.TH GTK-CONFIG 1 "November 2026" "CGTK @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtk-config \- compiler and linker flags for programs built with CGTK
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtk-config
.RB [ \-\-prefix [\fB=\fIDIR\fR]]
.RB [ \-\-exec\-prefix [\fB=\fIDIR\fR]]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-cflags ]
.RB [ \-\-libs ]
.RI [ library ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtk-config
prints the flags a C compiler and linker need to build a program with
CGTK, the Classic GUI Toolkit, which keeps the API of GTK+ 1.2.
It is the script GTK+ 1.2 had, kept so that makefiles and configure
scripts written for GTK+ 1.2 build against CGTK unchanged.
.PP
It answers from the pkg-config files installed with CGTK, so it and
.B \%pkg-config
always agree: the
.B gtk
library is
.IR gtk+-1.4 ,
.B gthread
adds
.I gthread-1.4
and
.B gtkgl
adds
.IR gtkgl-1.4 .
A new program can ask
.B \%pkg-config
for those names itself.
.B glib-config
does the same for GLib alone.
.SH OPTIONS
The options can be given in any order, and each that prints something
prints it on a line of its own.
.TP
.B \-\-cflags
Print the flags to compile with: where the headers are.
.TP
.B \-\-libs
Print the flags to link with: the libraries and where they are.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version of CGTK that is installed, and nothing else.
.TP
.B \-\-prefix
Print the prefix CGTK was installed under.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix= DIR
Print the flags for CGTK as if it were installed under
.I DIR
instead, for a copy that was moved after it was built.
It is the exec prefix as well, unless
.B \-\-exec\-prefix
is given too.
.TP
.B \-\-exec\-prefix
Print the exec prefix CGTK was installed under.
.TP
.BI \-\-exec\-prefix= DIR
Take
.I DIR
as the exec prefix.
.SH LIBRARIES
With no library named,
.B gtk
is meant.
.TP
.B gtk
GLib, GModule, GDK and GTK+.
.TP
.B gthread
GTK+ and GLib's threads: GThread.
.TP
.B gtkgl
GTK+ and GtkGLArea, the OpenGL widget, where CGTK was built with it.
The library OpenGL itself is in is not given, as a window system's is
not either: the program links that itself, usually by
.BR "pkg-config \-\-libs opengl" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
1 when it is run with nothing on its command line, an option or a
library is not known, or
pkg-config cannot find what was asked for; the reason is printed on
standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG
The pkg-config program to run;
.B \%pkg-config
if it is not set.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_PATH
Where else to look for pkg-config files. The directory CGTK installed
its own in is looked in first.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a program:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cc `gtk-config \-\-cflags` hello.c \-o hello `gtk-config \-\-libs`
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build one that draws with OpenGL:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cc `gtk-config \-\-cflags gtkgl` cube.c \-o cube \e
    `gtk-config \-\-libs gtkgl` `pkg-config \-\-libs opengl`
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg-config (1),
.BR cgtk-theme (1)
.PP
The README and INSTALL files of CGTK, and the AM_PATH_GTK macro of
.IR gtk.m4 ,
which configure scripts use.
